 "provenance": {
  "bevel": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "photo-measured - the housing is an octagon in section: the four edges that run from the port face to the back are cut off, which is what the user and the photographs call its wedge. The front's silhouette (front image, 4.407 px/mm) narrows 10.9 mm at its top and bottom rows and reaches full width 16.3 mm in, at every corner; the four product images give identical silhouettes, quantised to 1.8 mm by the image's mask, so 11 and 16 are good to about two millimetres. The video (0:31-0:41) shows these cuts running the whole depth. THE GREY BANDS BESIDE THE LEGEND PLATE ARE BEVELS TOO, which a first draft of this model read as flat casting and the maintainer corrected from the explorer: in the video's three-quarter frames (0:29-0:33, and the render at 0:46) the band right of the plate is lit as its own plane and its top edge slants up to meet the top face, and the back face (0:32) carries the same band between the plates and the fins. So the four edges between the front or back and the finned sides are bevelled as well, 12.6 mm across the face - the dark plate is 58.4 of the 83.8 mm, measured on the straight-on front - and taken at 45 degrees, because no view shows how far back along the side the bevel runs. The back is taken to match the front."
  },
  "bottom-layout": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - the underside is not photographed. Drawn as plain casting, the bevels strips at its sides; registered as a gap."
  },
  "chassis": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "datasheet - 'Dimension (L*W*H) 5.71 x 4.33 x 3.30 in'. The letters are not width, height and depth: the straight-on front reads 0.587 wide-to-tall against 3.30/5.71 = 0.578, so L (145.0 mm) is the face's height as the unit hangs on the rail, H (83.8) its width and W (110.0) the depth from the port face to the DIN face."
  },
  "front-layout": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "photo-measured on the straight-on AIS2004 front image at 4.407 px/mm (Gate 1: the face's own width agrees with the datasheet to 1.5 percent; the datasheet's front is the same artwork). Jack lamps located by colour; columns at x 23.2 and 44.7, rows on a 15.5 mm pitch from y 44.3. The SFP 2x2 block (9-12) sits where the AIS4001's does; the right-hand columns (13-16, 17-20) are four cages each at x 49.9-59.9, laid on one 14.5 mm pitch (the cage itself) from y 14.0 and 77.8 - the image's two gold strips measure 58.5 and 55.6 mm, which a 14.5 mm cage cannot honour both of, so the cages abut and each lamp sits at its cage's centre (the dashes read 22.0/36.6/50.7/64.9 and 85.5/99.4/112.9/126.3). Jacks are drawn with the lamped ganged cell turned 90/270 so the keyways face out; its lamps are 8.3 mm apart against the jacks' 11.5, the closest library cell that fits the 11 mm column. The console is the bare ganged cell, turned the same way. Cages are std/sfp@1 on their side; each SFP lamp is a small dash drawn with common/led-rect-sm@1 turned 90."
  },
  "lamps": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "photo-measured - each jack has ONE lamp, green, at its top (the PoE builds add an amber one below it), and the colour key names only LINK/ACT; drawn with common/rj45-ganged-link@1, the right-hand column drawn with its lamp-right skin so its lamp also lands at the top."
  },
  "power": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "datasheet - 'Power Supply DC 12-55 V'; 'Idling: 12V 6.13W / 55V 7.09W'; 'Full load: 12V 15.96W / 55V 17.49W'. power-max-w takes the highest figure (17.49 W); no ambient is stated with any of them. The supply is not included ('the power supply is excluded from the package')."
  },
  "rear-layout": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - the back render is foreshortened top to bottom; widths are taken as fractions of the face on the same image row, heights as fractions of 145 mm. Two wall plates (upper with its screws above the keyholes, lower with them below) and the DIN clip between them, centred. The DIN rail's centre line lies about 79 mm from the top of this face."
  },
  "relay-orientation": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "photo-measured - the two-position RELAY header is placed turned 90, its two contacts running front to back, parallel to the five of the power header, with its keyed, open side toward the RELAY legend as the power header's is toward the POWER legend. Read off the AurCore product video (frames at 0:34 and 1:02, the AIS4001P top face close up) and the vendor's AIS4001P and AIS2001 product images 2 (three-quarter) and 3 (back render), which show the same on both housings. It is placed at the centre it had unturned, 1.0 left of the old `at` because the header is now 12.16 wide, the Phoenix Contact MSTBA 2,5/ 2-G-5,08 width (#804)."
  },
  "sfp-numbering": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "photo-measured - the 2x2 block's strip reads as the AIS4001's (9 and 11 the right-hand column, 10 and 12 the left, by its arrows); the right-hand strips number 13-16 and 17-20 top to bottom, one lamp each. The GbE rows read '1v ^2' and so on, odd ports on the left by the same reading of the arrows."
  },
  "side-layout": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - from the video (0:37-0:41, 0:55) and the three-quarter image: both sides are fins running front to back, with a recessed channel and a raised badge plate carrying the wordmark on the right side. The left side is not photographed square on and is drawn as fins only."
  },
  "silkscreen": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "photo-measured - legends transcribed from the AIS2004 front image: Reset, SYS, PWR; Fast Ring and SCP with leaders to switches 1 and 2; CONSOLE; the port numbers as printed; LINK/ACT under its colour key (no PoE key on this build); the summary line '8 x GE | 12 x GE SFP'. The AURCORE wordmark is printed as text: its A is drawn as a chevron mark, which is not reproduced (no logo marks)."
  },
  "sources": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "vendor datasheet (AIS2004 Data Sheet 1.0, 3 pages: spec table, and an annotated front and back figure that is the same artwork as the product images); the product page's three images (straight-on front, three-quarter front-top-right, and a back render raised to show the top face), 1000 px; and the vendor's AIS4000 Series video (YouTube MfK6WpjLsA8, 1080p), whose footage at 0:28-1:02 is a real AIS4001P, the same housing - the top, back and sides here are that unit's, with the AIS2004's own power legend. No hardware guide or drawing is published (the Download Center holds the CLI, ACC and ACN manuals only)."
  },
  "top-layout": {
